From 094017205956cb94214e6e56cad7b539e4266cd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: footbolvovaukrnet77-glitch
 <footbolvovaukrnet77-glitch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:37:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(xbox): xgr IXGameUiImpl2 and IXGameUiImpl3 on the
 current runtime

Brings the ten methods of draft #63 (Micolash21) onto the current
xbox-series runtime, which gained title UI callbacks and handle tracking
after #63 was opened:

- XGameUiShowMultiplayerActivityGameInviteAsync/Result go to the title's
  showMultiplayerActivityGameInviteCallback when one is set (answered by
  XGameUiSetMultiplayerActivityGameInviteUiResponse), else E_ABORT.
- XGameUiShowStateShareAsync/Result: no callback exists in
  XGameUiUiCallbacks, so always headless (E_ABORT).
- XGameUiTextEntryOpen/Close/GetState/GetExtents/UpdatePositionHint/
  UpdateVisibility: #63's headless keyboard (first GetState reports
  Dismissed with the initial text), now reported to XSystemHandleTrack
  and XSystemIsHandleValid as GameUiTextEntry; the track callback runs
  outside the text entry lock.

Tests move to test_ui.cpp (callback, headless and handle tracking
cases). xgr_status.json: 398 of 398; progress.svg regenerated.

Original text entry design: Micolash21 (#63).
Built with MinGW-w64; the Windows CI job runs test_ui.
